.TH CARDEA-TEAM 1 "2026-11-23" "cardea-kernel" "Cardea"
.SH NAME
cardea-team \- run the Cardea agent dev team from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cardea team
[\fB\-\-host\fR \fIFILE\fR]
.I COMMAND
[\fIARGUMENTS\fR]
.br
.B cardea team \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cardea team
runs a deployed agent dev team (the team kit, ADR-034) as its supervisor: it shows the team's
state, pauses and resumes it, changes its settings and mails its roles. The commands are the
team kit's own, installed under
.IR /usr/lib/cardea/teamkit ;
the kernel's code does the work, and the kernel alone decides whether the supervisor may.
.PP
It works as a plain user. Every command acts through the team's host file, so it runs as the
.B cardea\-kernel
account that owns that file and the supervisor's identity. A member of the
.B cardea\-operators
group is let through by one rule in
.IR /etc/sudoers.d/cardea\-team ,
which allows only the root-owned helper
.I /usr/libexec/cardea\-team
to run as
.BR cardea\-kernel ,
with no arguments. The request is sent on the helper's standard input. The helper reads only the
fixed host file
.IR /etc/cardea/team.host.json ;
\fB\-\-host\fR is honoured only when the caller already is
.BR cardea\-kernel .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
The team overview: members and their runs, work by state, mail, approvals, spend and run ceilings,
when the credentials expire, and the last failed runs. While the team is paused it prints the
pause reason and the failures recorded then.
.TP
\fBpause\fR [\fIreason\fR]
Cancel every unfinished run and admit nothing until
.BR resume .
The reason is kept for
.BR status ;
put no secret in it.
.TP
.B resume
Enable the supervisor again, so triggers admit.
.TP
.B stop
Pause, then delete the group; its members drain. Collections and records stay.
.TP
.B apply
Put the collections and the group to the kernel as the supervisor.
.TP
\fBrender\fR [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIDIR\fR]
Write the documents the team is made of, for review. The default directory is
.IR /var/lib/cardea/team/rendered ;
through the helper, only directories below
.I /var/lib/cardea/team
are accepted.
.TP
\fBprovision\fR [\fB\-\-paused\fR]
Merge the team's principals and grants into the provisioning document and provision the kernel
with it. Refused while the team is paused unless \fB\-\-paused\fR is given.
.TP
\fBsettings\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR]
Show the settings as they are now: run limits, spend limits, pause, schedules, developers,
email rate limit, model and product goals (goals by size only).
.TP
\fBset\fR [\fB\-y\fR] [\fB\-\-confirm\fR \fITOKEN\fR] \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR
Change one setting. The change is validated as the dashboard Settings page validates it, the
difference is shown, and you are asked before anything is applied. What is applied is exactly
what was shown: if the host file changed in between, nothing is applied.
.B \-y
applies without asking; \fB\-\-confirm\fR applies a preview whose token an earlier run printed.
.I KEY
is a setting field such as
.BR developers ,
.BR model ,
.BR run_limits.team ,
.BR run_limits.roles.dev ,
.BR spend_limits.per_run_usd ,
.BR email_rate_limit.count ,
.BR schedules.pm ,
.BR paused ,
.BR product_goals.goals .
.I VALUE
is JSON (a number, true, false, a list or an object); text settings take the text as it is;
a schedule is cron expressions separated by semicolons. Every attempt is recorded in the team's
settings audit.
.TP
\fBmail\fR \fITARGET\fR \fITEXT\fR
Mail a role, as the supervisor.
.I TARGET
is
.BR tl ,
.BR pm ,
.BR pe ,
.B ux
or
.BI dev. N
for the developer numbered from 0.
.TP
\fBmail list\fR [\fB\-\-member\fR \fIID\fR] [\fB\-\-item\fR \fICOLLECTION/ID\fR] [\fB\-\-after\fR \fICURSOR\fR] [\fB\-\-limit\fR \fIN\fR]
List the team's mail, newest first.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/cardea/team.host.json
The host file: the namespace, the supervisor's identity, the repository, credential names, model
and budgets (an example is in
.IR /usr/share/doc/cardea\-kernel/team.host.example.json ).
Keep it owned by
.B cardea\-kernel
and private (mode 0600); it may sit in the root-owned
.IR /etc/cardea ,
where a settings change rewrites it in place.
.TP
.I /var/lib/cardea/team
Where the kit keeps the provisioning document it writes, the pause record and the settings
audit, unless the host file's \fBprovisioning\fR section says otherwise.
.TP
.I /etc/sudoers.d/cardea\-team
The one rule: members of \fBcardea\-operators\fR may run \fI/usr/libexec/cardea\-team\fR as
\fBcardea\-kernel\fR, with no arguments.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 when the command or the kernel refused; 2 for a usage error or a change left
unconfirmed.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cardea (1),
.IR /usr/share/doc/cardea\-kernel/README.md
